It's low in these
branched chain amino acids

00:27:29.820 --> 00:27:30.958
that I've mentioned.
- Okay.

00:27:30.958 --> 00:27:34.310
[stammers] a diet that mimics fasting

00:27:34.310 --> 00:27:38.120
or does that include periods
of actually not taking

00:27:38.120 --> 00:27:39.490
in any calories?

00:27:39.490 --> 00:27:41.040
- It's both but you don't have to be

00:27:41.040 --> 00:27:43.680
as rigorous about the period.

00:27:43.680 --> 00:27:45.000
The food itself will-

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:49.230
- So the food itself is
being processed by your body

00:27:49.230 --> 00:27:50.580
in such a way that the body is like,

00:27:50.580 --> 00:27:52.530
I could really use a little bit more,

00:27:52.530 --> 00:27:54.280
I could really like a little bit more.

00:27:54.280 --> 00:27:56.020
- Yeah, you want them, to the body to be

00:27:56.020 --> 00:27:57.780
in a state of perceived adversity.

00:27:57.780 --> 00:27:59.790
Oh my goodness, I'm running out of food.

00:27:59.790 --> 00:28:01.480
I'm not eating meat anymore

00:28:01.480 --> 00:28:03.240
because plants have less
of these amino acids.

00:28:03.240 --> 00:28:08.240
So it responds to that
low amino acid input.

00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:10.880
Valter's done some great
work, over the last few years,

00:28:10.880 --> 00:28:12.900
he and his group have shown

00:28:12.900 --> 00:28:15.060
that on this fasting mimicking diet,

00:28:15.060 --> 00:28:16.660
which they can send you at home,

00:28:17.810 --> 00:28:20.540
that actually helps
cancer patients survive

00:28:20.540 --> 00:28:23.140
and get over chemotherapy quicker.

00:28:23.140 --> 00:28:26.540
Again, more evidence that fasting is good,

00:28:26.540 --> 00:28:28.850
not just for longevity but for diseases.

00:28:28.850 --> 00:28:30.790
So that's one, the next one let's talk

00:28:30.790 --> 00:28:33.520
about which a lot of people
call intermittent fasting.

00:28:33.520 --> 00:28:34.870
We'll just call it fasting.

00:28:35.810 --> 00:28:38.320
This is a period, if you
go longer than a day,

00:28:38.320 --> 00:28:41.220
some people do three days,
some people go for a week.

00:28:41.220 --> 00:28:42.230
I wouldn't go longer than that

00:28:42.230 --> 00:28:43.630
'cause then you'll start
chewing up your muscle,

00:28:43.630 --> 00:28:44.860
which you don't want to do.

00:28:44.860 --> 00:28:46.980
But these long extended periods

00:28:46.980 --> 00:28:49.200
are doing a real deep cleanse on the body

00:28:49.200 --> 00:28:50.710
and turning on that autophagy,

00:28:50.710 --> 00:28:53.280
that process of recycling
proteins very deeply.

00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:55.730
Especially, once you get
beyond the three-day mark,

00:28:55.730 --> 00:28:58.410
when your metabolism
switches into what's called

00:28:58.410 --> 00:29:01.790
chaperone-mediated
autophagy, the deep cleanse.

00:29:01.790 --> 00:29:04.320
So that's fasting and then
there's time restricted feeding,

00:29:04.320 --> 00:29:06.300
which is what I do,
'cause I'm not very good

00:29:06.300 --> 00:29:07.410
at going beyond 24 hours.

00:29:07.410 --> 00:29:10.700
- Well, [mumbles] think most
people would really struggle

00:29:10.700 --> 00:29:12.040
to get there.
- Yeah,

00:29:12.040 --> 00:29:14.250
time restricted feeding,
which is what I do,

00:29:14.250 --> 00:29:16.450
which is, try not to eat till dinner.

00:29:16.450 --> 00:29:18.920
That's hard enough, my hats off to people

00:29:18.920 --> 00:29:21.601
like Peter [indistinct],
the [indistinct] podcast,

00:29:21.601 --> 00:29:24.610
[indistinct] many of our
audience will have heard of,

00:29:24.610 --> 00:29:28.430
he can go for a week and
he's got a lot of willpower.

00:29:28.430 --> 00:29:31.540
If you've ever met the guy,
he's different than me.

00:29:31.540 --> 00:29:32.430
I'm more of a hedonist,

00:29:32.430 --> 00:29:33.700
but he
- Is he grumpier

00:29:33.700 --> 00:29:34.900
at the end of the week, do you think

00:29:34.900 --> 00:29:36.400
than he is at the beginning
of the week though?

00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:38.310
I mean, like after all of that time.

00:29:38.310 --> 00:29:39.480
- He's always serious.

00:29:39.480 --> 00:29:42.440
That's what I can tell you, but brilliant.

00:29:42.440 --> 00:29:45.433
But let get back to this
time-restricted feeding.

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:49.330
You want to have at least 16 hours

00:29:49.330 --> 00:29:52.620
of not eating or not eating very much.

00:29:52.620 --> 00:29:53.710
And then you can have eight hours.

00:29:53.710 --> 00:29:55.530
So typically that means
having a late lunch,

00:29:55.530 --> 00:29:57.430
if you skip breakfast or if you prefer

00:29:57.430 --> 00:29:59.350
to skip dinner, I'd skip that.

00:29:59.350 --> 00:30:00.753
- Because we [mumbles] remember here is

00:30:00.753 --> 00:30:03.440
that there's a period of sleep
in which you are not eating.

00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:04.670
And so,
- That's the easy part.

00:30:04.670 --> 00:30:06.840
what you're really doing
is tacking on hours

00:30:06.840 --> 00:30:07.880
to the front of that

00:30:07.880 --> 00:30:09.750
and tacking on hours to the back of that.

00:30:09.750 --> 00:30:11.640
- That's right, so when
people say I'm skipping lunch,

00:30:11.640 --> 00:30:13.580
that's not as helpful.

00:30:13.580 --> 00:30:15.190
And so what I've done in my life,

00:30:15.190 --> 00:30:19.410
let's just use me as an example
of an average human being.

00:30:19.410 --> 00:30:22.883
'Cause I'm pretty lazy
and I'm not that driven.

00:30:24.170 --> 00:30:26.870
I prefer to take a pill,
which is not the right thing.

00:30:27.830 --> 00:30:31.000
What I started out in my life
was not to eat breakfast.

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:34.680
And pretty much been doing
that since I was a teenager.

00:30:34.680 --> 00:30:36.920
And that for me works
because I'm not really hungry

00:30:36.920 --> 00:30:39.010
in the morning, I have a cup
of tea or a cup of coffee,

00:30:39.010 --> 00:30:40.220
and I still do that,

00:30:40.220 --> 00:30:42.300
a little bit of yogurt to
mix my supplements with,

00:30:42.300 --> 00:30:43.427
to dissolve them.
- And you're not taking,

00:30:43.427 --> 00:30:44.860
you're not doing the yogurt.

00:30:44.860 --> 00:30:46.370
And I've actually seen you do this.

00:30:46.370 --> 00:30:47.720
The amount of yogurt that you put

00:30:47.720 --> 00:30:49.710
into your little bowl is really minimal.

00:30:49.710 --> 00:30:51.450
It's basically just to mix up

00:30:51.450 --> 00:30:52.740
your-
- a couple of spoons.

00:30:52.740 --> 00:30:54.370
- Yeah.
- That's it.

00:30:54.370 --> 00:30:56.460
And that's burnt off in 15 minutes.

00:30:56.460 --> 00:30:59.100
So it's not going to be a big
deal for the rest of the day.

00:30:59.100 --> 00:31:01.320
And I try not to eat at all until dinner.

00:31:01.320 --> 00:31:05.180
And then I have a really
enjoyable, largish dinner,

00:31:05.180 --> 00:31:06.560
but it's certain types of food.

00:31:06.560 --> 00:31:08.460
We'll talk about the types of food later,

00:31:08.460 --> 00:31:10.653
but that gives my body this long window,

00:31:11.670 --> 00:31:15.680
more than 20 hours of not
having glucose circulating

00:31:15.680 --> 00:31:17.770
from the external world.

00:31:17.770 --> 00:31:19.580
Now what happens when you do that?

00:31:19.580 --> 00:31:21.780
And it takes a few weeks
for your body to adapt,

00:31:21.780 --> 00:31:24.920
is that your liver will
learn how to compensate

00:31:24.920 --> 00:31:26.120
for lack of food.

00:31:26.120 --> 00:31:28.270
It's called gluconeogenesis,

00:31:28.270 --> 00:31:30.450
the generation of glucose from your liver.

00:31:30.450 --> 00:31:34.100
And it actually overcomes
the feeling of hunger.

00:31:34.100 --> 00:31:36.060
When you first skip breakfast and lunch,

00:31:36.060 --> 00:31:36.893
you're going to be hungry.

00:31:36.893 --> 00:31:38.210
You're going to be nervous,
you're going to say,

00:31:38.210 --> 00:31:39.900
I can't do this, Sinclair is an idiot.

00:31:39.900 --> 00:31:41.470
- Well, this is why people fail at this,

00:31:41.470 --> 00:31:44.220
is because they run into
that and they think,

00:31:44.220 --> 00:31:46.010
this is how life is
going to be for the rest

00:31:46.010 --> 00:31:47.170
of the time that I'm on this diet.

00:31:47.170 --> 00:31:48.210
I can't do this diet.

00:31:48.210 --> 00:31:50.150
- Right, but do it for at least two weeks.

00:31:50.150 --> 00:31:51.320
Because after the two week,

00:31:51.320 --> 00:31:52.480
especially by the three week mark,

00:31:52.480 --> 00:31:54.050
your liver has now learned

00:31:54.050 --> 00:31:55.590
that you're not going
to breakfast or lunch,

00:31:55.590 --> 00:31:59.290
and it will start making
glucose at a steady level.

00:31:59.290 --> 00:32:00.940
That's really important because

00:32:02.090 --> 00:32:04.300
it's known that if you have
these spikes of glucose,

00:32:04.300 --> 00:32:08.590
it leads to hunger when it
crashes after a big meal,

00:32:08.590 --> 00:32:10.610
but also that when you
get hungry, you eat.

00:32:10.610 --> 00:32:12.933
So you're in this wave of hungry, eating-

00:32:14.190 --> 00:32:15.550
- Do you think people should ramp up,

00:32:15.550 --> 00:32:16.590
I mean, you said like,

00:32:16.590 --> 00:32:19.250
do no breakfast and lunch for two weeks

00:32:19.250 --> 00:32:21.570
but should they ramp up
by like breakfast first

00:32:21.570 --> 00:32:25.120
and let their liver get
used to compensating

00:32:25.120 --> 00:32:28.340
for no breakfast and then add lunch?

00:32:28.340 --> 00:32:29.560
- Well, I would skip one meal

00:32:29.560 --> 00:32:30.570
and then go for two.
- Yeah.

00:32:30.570 --> 00:32:31.890
- You can't do the whole thing.

00:32:31.890 --> 00:32:33.860
Most people will fail,

00:32:33.860 --> 00:32:36.190
but you're trying to avoid
this thing I was just talking

00:32:36.190 --> 00:32:38.570
about called reactive hypoglycemia,

00:32:38.570 --> 00:32:40.570
is that if you eat a piece
of toast for breakfast

00:32:40.570 --> 00:32:44.160
or heaven forbid, a giant
glass of orange juice,

00:32:44.160 --> 00:32:46.740
you'll have this spike in
sugar and you'll feel great,

00:32:46.740 --> 00:32:49.170
but then your body will
put out too much insulin

00:32:49.170 --> 00:32:51.630
and suck that glucose
out of your bloodstream

00:32:51.630 --> 00:32:55.400
and put you into a glucose
deficit and that's hypoglycemia.

00:32:55.400 --> 00:32:57.310
And then you're hungry,
you've got ghrelin coming out

00:32:57.310 --> 00:32:59.640
into your body and you feel hungry

00:32:59.640 --> 00:33:01.320
and you need eat something.

00:33:01.320 --> 00:33:02.330
I'm at a state though,

00:33:02.330 --> 00:33:04.270
now, where I don't get
those rises and crashes.

00:33:04.270 --> 00:33:06.090
My liver is putting out glucose

00:33:06.090 --> 00:33:08.530
from when I wake up till dinner.

00:33:08.530 --> 00:33:10.210
And I've never been so focused.

00:33:10.210 --> 00:33:15.120
I've never been so brain fog free

00:33:15.120 --> 00:33:16.230
because these crashes,

00:33:16.230 --> 00:33:18.420
what they do is they make you feel shaky

00:33:18.420 --> 00:33:20.730
or tired and brain fog.

00:33:20.730 --> 00:33:22.257
And I wish I'd done this in my 20s

00:33:22.257 --> 00:33:23.500
and done it my whole life,

00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:26.090
because I've really never
felt better, because of it.

00:33:26.090 --> 00:33:28.200
